<!--Post: 4889--><!--Time: 1106795624-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4889"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 7:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax, I agree. It could be argued that BTK is deliberately withholding powerful proof &#40;ie. definitive evidence of at least one more victim, perhaps Hedge, Baker or Davis&#41; until folks believe he&#39;s turned in all his material, upon which time BTK drops another bomb similar to Vicki Wegerle. I don&#39;t think this will to be the case. <BR> <BR>I think all of BTK&#39;s victims are known, we know them all right now, but BTK still has enough material to play around with, at least a few more &#34;drops&#34; worth of information. I must also wonder if BTK is in the least bit ill. He may not be and I&#39;ve seen no evidence that he is terminal. Some fairly sweet offers have been made to him, I wish he&#39;d seriously consider one or two of them while he has the chance.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
